WEBVTT

00:00:00.127 --> 00:00:02.456
{happy}Hello, and welcome to Shah Spectrum.

00:00:02.456 --> 00:00:08.131
Today's story is about an exam, a pair of glasses, and a minister who stepped down.

00:00:08.131 --> 00:00:14.184
{happy}Imagine sitting the most important exam of your life, and the person at the

00:00:14.184 --> 00:00:18.731
next desk may be wearing glasses that can read the question and find the answer.

00:00:18.731 --> 00:00:19.613
Could anyone tell?

00:00:19.613 --> 00:00:21.729
South Korea has just had to face that question.

00:00:21.729 --> 00:00:26.870
{happy}I'm Mittal Shah, and today I'll walk you through how an AI cheating scandal

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.295
ended with a government minister resigning, and what it says about exams everywhere.

00:00:32.295 --> 00:00:33.955
{fluent}First, the exam.

00:00:33.955 --> 00:00:38.700
On Thursday the nineteenth of November, roughly half a million students sat South

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.554
Korea's national college entrance test, called the Suneung.

00:00:42.554 --> 00:00:45.504
It is a single national exam taken on one day.

00:00:45.504 --> 00:00:47.477
The country goes quiet for it.

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:51.990
Flights are held back during the listening section, and stock trading is delayed.

00:00:52.482 --> 00:00:53.891
Now, the scandal.

00:00:53.891 --> 00:00:58.988
On Sunday the fifteenth, a man who had topped the national tax accountant exam said,

00:00:58.988 --> 00:01:02.302
in a video posted by his lawyer, how he did it.

00:01:02.302 --> 00:01:07.801
He says he photographed the questions with a tiny camera, sent them to generative

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:13.049
AI, which is software that writes answers to questions, and read the answers on his

00:01:13.049 --> 00:01:13.649
phone.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:18.680
He says he used the same method on another professional exam, and that he has turned

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:19.280
himself in.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.400
A police unit has been assigned.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:26.149
Reports also describe test-takers caught with AI smart glasses, which are glasses

00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:31.519
with a built-in camera and an AI assistant, on an English test in June and on some

00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:34.453
university essay exams in October.

00:01:35.006 --> 00:01:38.156
So what did the government do?

00:01:38.156 --> 00:01:42.049
On Monday the sixteenth, Education Minister Choi Kyo-jin told lawmakers that

00:01:42.049 --> 00:01:44.973
AI-assisted cheating would be hard to catch in every form.

00:01:44.973 --> 00:01:51.692
He declined calls to postpone the exam, saying a delay would cause an even larger

00:01:51.692 --> 00:01:52.583
disruption for students.

00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:56.064
Then, two days before the test, the ministry announced new rules.

00:01:56.064 --> 00:01:57.932
Glasses would be inspected.

00:01:57.932 --> 00:02:01.251
Shirt buttons would be covered and sleeves rolled up.

00:02:01.251 --> 00:02:05.754
Phones across the country would get random emergency-style alerts.

00:02:05.754 --> 00:02:08.069
And public Wi-Fi near test centres would be shut down.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.901
Here is why that was so difficult.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:16.189
Officials said metal and radio detectors, which pick up wireless signals, would be

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:16.789
limited.

00:02:16.758 --> 00:02:23.186
Thermal cameras, which sense body heat, were highly unlikely because of privacy

00:02:23.186 --> 00:02:23.786
concerns.

00:02:23.669 --> 00:02:27.310
Jamming, meaning blocking phone signals, is prohibited.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:32.983
And an opposition spokesperson said radio detectors had failed to detect AI glasses

00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:33.891
in a mock test.

00:02:34.277 --> 00:02:39.458
After the exam, the ministry said a hundred and eleven people were suspected of

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:44.433
using electronic devices, and fifty-four of those cases were flagged through the

00:02:44.433 --> 00:02:45.377
phone alerts.

00:02:45.377 --> 00:02:49.150
A task force is still reviewing Wi-Fi and Bluetooth signals.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:53.938
On Sunday the twenty-second, the minister announced his resignation.

00:02:53.938 --> 00:03:00.069
One report says he pointed to public criticism over how early the ministry prepared.

00:03:00.382 --> 00:03:01.097
So, could anyone tell?

00:03:01.097 --> 00:03:02.343
Partly.

00:03:02.343 --> 00:03:06.802
The phone alerts flagged fifty-four cases, but detectors have limits, and the full

00:03:06.802 --> 00:03:08.124
review is still under way.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:11.124
Now, why does one score matter so much?

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:16.589
One report puts private tutoring in South Korea at about twenty-seven and a half

00:03:16.589 --> 00:03:20.605
trillion won in twenty twenty-five, roughly twenty billion dollars.

00:03:20.605 --> 00:03:23.237
That shows how much rides on a single result.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:28.149
As for what comes next, on the twentieth, President Lee Jae-myung called for a

00:03:28.149 --> 00:03:31.367
sweeping overhaul of national exams.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:36.390
Seoul's city education office put forward a plan last December to phase the Suneung

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.198
out by the twenty-forty school year.

00:03:38.198 --> 00:03:41.606
The national government has not adopted that plan.

00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:43.501
So what do we not know?

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:49.487
We do not know how many of the hundred and eleven suspected cases will be confirmed.

00:03:49.487 --> 00:03:53.797
One proposal would ban cheaters from retaking the exam for years.

00:03:53.797 --> 00:03:56.024
It is a proposal, not a law.

00:03:56.024 --> 00:04:01.370
And the government says AI companies will provide records to investigators, but none

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.476
has been named.

00:04:02.476 --> 00:04:03.538
{happy}To sum up:

00:04:03.538 --> 00:04:07.805
AI can now answer almost any question on a page, and catching it is hard.

00:04:07.805 --> 00:04:13.383
So South Korea is asking what a fair test should measure when answers are cheap.

00:04:13.383 --> 00:04:16.169
It may be a question for every exam.

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:19.258
{happy}Thanks for listening, and see you in the next episode!

